# A Luxel library scene — Apache-2.0. Grammar: library/README.md.
# Sprites on the march: a smiley that HOPS (an `out` key up to the apex, an
# `in` key back down, so it hangs at the top and drops), a face cycling its
# moods and an alien shuffling with a sine bob, all on one street. Every
# track is a conveyor on one 8 s loop
# (docs/spec/scenes.md "Keyframes"): the parade moves 10 px/s, a key every
# second, and the two keys sharing one ms are the instant jump from the
# right edge back to the left, made while the sprite is off screen.
# Authored for 64x64; the sprites are 16 px or smaller, so on a 32x32 the
# same parade crosses the top-left quarter with the street out of frame.
S - Sprite Parade
L pat 0 0 0 0 normal 100 none fill 1
N Sky
I @pat/color-wash
L color 0 52 0 12 normal 100 none fill 1
N Street
K 2a2238
L color 0 52 0 1 normal 100 none fill 1
N Curb
K 7a6a9e
L sprite 4 44 0 0 normal 100 none fill 1
N Alien
I @spr/pixel-alien
M 0 4 44 = linear
M 1000 14 42 = sine
M 2000 24 44 = sine
M 3000 34 42 = sine
M 4000 44 44 = sine
M 5000 54 42 = sine
M 6000 64 44 = sine
M 6000 -16 44 = step
M 7000 -6 42 = sine
M 8000 4 44 = sine
L sprite 24 36 0 0 normal 100 none fill 1
N Smiley
I @spr/smiley
M 0 24 36 = linear
M 1000 34 30 = out
M 2000 44 36 = in
M 3000 54 30 = out
M 4000 64 36 = in
M 4000 -16 36 = step
M 5000 -6 30 = out
M 6000 4 36 = in
M 7000 14 30 = out
M 8000 24 36 = in
L sprite 44 36 0 0 normal 100 none fill 1
N Moods
I @spr/face-moods
M 0 44 36 = linear
M 1000 54 34 = sine
M 2000 64 36 = sine
M 2000 -16 36 = step
M 3000 -6 34 = sine
M 4000 4 36 = sine
M 5000 14 34 = sine
M 6000 24 36 = sine
M 7000 34 34 = sine
M 8000 44 36 = sine
